                    <death when="1870-07-01"/>
                    <occupation>civil engineer</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Philip Taylor patented the application of high-pressure steam to evaporation and devised a method of making gas from oil.  He spent much of his later
  life in France and was made a knight of the French Légion d'honneur in 1846.  He was the son of <persName key="TAY02 TAY04">John and Susannah Taylor</persName> 
    of Norwich who also appear 
  in the diary.</p>
                        <p>'P Taylor' has been identified as Philip.</p>
                    </note>
